 # Usage Notes
 
 Copy the .zip from "Additional Files" to your Codex, Claude Code, or other harness, or add the .zip to a project knowledge base in Chat. Attach or reference the .zip in chat and say, "Install this Augment." The prompt in this post is optional.
 
-Ask "What knowledge collections do we already have?" or "Find the archive for this topic." Giles can show registered stores and their exact routes before reading the needed sources. Open `skills/rupert-giles-knowledge-steward/Open Giles.cmd` in the plugin, or use its `.command` counterpart. The catalog starts empty on a new customer installation; add the stores you own or import your exported catalog. No private archive or source content is shipped.
+Ask “What knowledge collections do we already have?” or name a half-remembered subject. For the optional visual route, extract the complete edition and open `skills/rupert-giles-knowledge-steward/Open Giles.cmd` inside the chosen host plugin. Python 3.10+ must already be available; the neighboring `.command` is the supplied macOS/Linux route. Follow the Giles journey in `docs/VISUAL-WORKSPACES.md` to register one store, verify its save, select an entry point and copy the retrieval brief into Nova. Keep the same external catalog path when upgrading.
 
-Use the included VISUAL-WORKSPACES.md to select the matching launcher and artifact. Project Bridge and OMNARA use their native save/export paths. AnswerLayer and Beryl prepare in-memory working JSON: download before closing or reloading, then reopen the saved file. Observatory is read-only; Knowledge Desk reads only when you choose Read owner and never writes records. Labeled examples are teaching data, not your devices, research or people.
+Use `Export catalog` to back up descriptions and locators, and back up source archives separately. Import merges store IDs and stops on differing existing records until you explicitly choose replacement. A stale save needs `Reload` and inspection before retry. `Remove catalog record` leaves the source untouched. A description does not prove reading and a location check does not certify freshness.
+
+Use the workspace guide for the other owners' save and read boundaries. Project Bridge and OMNARA save native records. AnswerLayer and Beryl keep working JSON in memory: download before closing or reloading, then reopen it. Observatory is read-only; Knowledge Desk reads only when you choose `Read owner`. Labeled examples are teaching data.
 
 The separate persona prompt can also be used as a standalone prompt.
 
